endpoints_a.etym_text:
Uncertain. There are several theories:
* Inherited from Old Norse álpt (“swan”);
* Borrowed from Finnish ala- (“low”);
* Borrowed from Northern Sami álda (“sacrificial site”).
First attested in Danish in 1520 as Althen.

